``
So the bug is in my quick parser, not the anchors. The parser bug: `re` unused, and for hunks I `continue` — fine — but the increment `rs++` happens for every line starting with '+' INCLUDING the `+++ b/...` header line and also context lines are not counted — wait, context lines (' ') and '-' lines must ALSO advance rs? No — rs (right-side counter) advances for '+' AND ' (context) lines only, not '-' lines. My parser only advanced rs on '+' lines — context lines didn't advance it. That desyncs the count, so 389/394 came out wrong.

Let me fix the parser: advance rs for lines starting with '+' (not '+++') or ' (space context), and skip '-' lines.

